          "do": "inspect",
          "title": "The Golden Age of Crappy Ideas",
          "text": "One piece of writing here is Skye’s own: “The Golden Age of Crappy Ideas,” published 10 August 2026. Her argument is that AI has made a mountain of overengineered ideas buildable, and has also let more people make useful, strange, personal things. Her example of the first kind is an agent setup built to check the weather: “Then you find out what the system actually does. It checks the weather.”",
          "kicker": "Discovery"
        }
      ],
      "doneWhen": {
        "discovered": "apt_books"
      }
    },
